- 손의 쇠막대가 필릿 용접 토우에 걸쳐 있다.
- 다음 볼트 구멍에 같은 발의 물기가 있다.
- 쇠막대 끝에서 철컥 소리가 나며 줄의 맨 끝에 그 발이 있다.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G20-heading-0023"></a>

## 서식권 기록

해무가 짙은 주의 밤에 선반 하부 도크의 강재가 젖어 있다. 볼트 구멍의 철편 사이에 인천신탁전구 염분 화물 포장 파편이 끼여 있으며 파편 위에 소금기가 하얗다. 파편이 끼인 구멍에서 철컥 소리가 난다.

도크 반입구에 접지 코일이 놓여 있다. 코일의 구리선이 도크 강재 필릿에 닿아 있으며 닿은 자리에 철편이 겹쳐 있다. 코일에 마포 연합 여의도출자연합회 표찰이 걸려 있다. 구리와 강재가 맞닿은 자리에서 철컥 소리가 난다.

선반의 철판이 하부 플랜지에 내려와 있다. 철판의 모서리가 불가사리 입에 물려 있으며 남은 철판이 가슴의 철편 아래에 깔려 있다. 철판의 구멍은 플랜지 볼트선과 맞닿아 있다.

볼트선 위의 철컥이는 구멍 하나씩 떨어져 엎드려 있다. 한가운데 자리는 플랜지 위의 불가사리이며 끝 구멍은 앵글의 한 발이다. 두두리의 무릎이 줄 앞 하부 볼트에 걸려 있다.

크레인 훅이 거더 위에 있으며 와이어가 웨브에 닿아 있다. 와이어가 판에 스칠 때마다 두두리의 등과 철편에서 소리가 겹친다. 훅의 안전핀이 상부 선반 함에 있다.

선반 하부 쇄정에 뚝섬 연합 자물쇠가 걸려 있다. 도크 야간 당직의 손이 상부 선반 함의 크레인 키 위에 있다. 함 뚜껑의 철편이 키 옆에 한 장 놓여 있다.

하부 발판이 상부 선반에 포개져 있으며 선반 당직의 장화가 그 발판 위에 나란하다. 야간 순찰의 손전등이 상부 난간에 걸려 있다. 상부 난간의 볼트선은 가득하다.

도크 난간에서 빠진 볼트가 용접 토우의 철편 더미에 있다. 도크 야간 당직의 예비 장화가 그 더미에 묻혀 있다. 예비 장화의 목이 철편 위로 나와 있다.
');
INSERT INTO wiki_document (slug, title, title_ko, category_id, sort, body_md, body_ko_md) VALUES ('Hostile-Group-G21', 'G21 · Wall-knocker', 'G21 · 벽두드리기', 'bestiary', 21, '<a id="Hostile-Group-G21-heading-0001"></a>

[Ecology and variant bestiary](/wiki/Hostile-Ecology-Index/)

<a id="Hostile-Group-G21-heading-0003"></a>

## Common species and variants

In the relay niche on an early winter night a person holds the brow to the duct wall on the heating-pipe side. The mouth and neck are wet, and the brow strikes the plate with each breath. The knocking of the people standing on the same wall is closer toward the junction.

Dueoksini''s head presses the upper end of the junction niche. The Nail-scratcher''s nails are in the groove at hand height below it. The Yagwanggwi''s blue light is in the dark stretch outside the niche, the Wall-knockers'' bodies are toward the junction, and their faces are toward the light.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G21-heading-0006"></a>

## Ecology

| Item | Record |
|---|---|
| Origin | The Eastern Command duct watch stands in front of the iron door of the relay niche in the underground duct of the Eastern Command on the Gwangjin Line. It is an early winter night. Inside the niche a person holds the brow to the duct wall. / The mouth and neck are wet, and a gurgle comes from the throat with each breath. At each outgoing breath the brow strikes the plate once. Both hands lie beside the rivets. Black plate grime lies on the fingertips. The chest is toward the joint where the heating pipe runs. |
| Habitat and movement | It is the relay niche in the underground duct of the Eastern Command on the Gwangjin Line. It is an early winter night. The wall-knockers are gathered at the duct wall inside the niche. Mouths and necks are wet, and a gurgle comes from the throat with each breath. Chests face the joint where the heating pipe runs. / The person toward the door strikes the plate once with the brow at each breath. The person in the middle strikes the rivets with both palms at a short interval. The person toward the junction has the chest flat to the duct wall. The knocking of the fingertips and the knocking of the brow ring the plate at the same interval. Black plate grime lies on the fingertips. / The Eastern Command duct watch stands in front of the niche''s iron door. The watch sets the latch of the iron door. The knocking travels through the iron door into the back of the watch''s hand. The watch has ear covers on and the back against the iron door. |
| Food and energy | Waterproof tape, a spare latch, and flashlight cells are divided from the relay box into the Eastern Command duct watch''s vest and onto the box lid. Over-gloves lie under the plate in front of the Nail-scratcher. The Amsa–Godeok merchant band''s repair sack is at the edge of the Yagwanggwi''s light. |
| Life cycle and upkeep | A person with a wet mouth and wet neck, a gurgle coming from the throat, holds the brow to the duct wall. At each outgoing breath the brow strikes the plate together with the gurgle. Black plate grime lies on the fingertips. |
| Senses | The Wall-knocker''s chest faces the joint plate, and the head is toward the plate where the knocking lingers. The palms lie on the rivet line. In the stretch where the Yagwanggwi stands, the face is turned toward the blue light. |
| Group behavior | Dueoksini is inside the junction niche. The Nail-scratcher is at the plate at hand height below Dueoksini. The Wall-knockers stand along the wall from the junction toward the door, and the Yagwanggwi is in the dark stretch outside the door. |

**Life in the endless cold.** Wall-knockers press against the heating-pipe side of duct walls. They follow warmth through the walls and knock with each breath, and the colder the night the more of them gather on the same warm wall.

**Threat and the cost of fighting.** Their knocking can mask alarms and draw others to the relay niche. The infected are a middle threat that grows in closed rooms. Infantry hold the doors in pairs, support teams bring medicine, isolation sheets and warm water, and missile infantry fire only when a line breaks. Recon drones are used to look into a room before anyone opens it, which saves lives but spends cells. War machines have no place here. The heaviest costs are medicine and the people who catch what they fight; ammunition spent on the infected is ammunition the station mourns later. Every watch knows the infected were people, and the duty log treats them that way.

<a id="Hostile-Group-G21-heading-0008"></a>

## Individuals and battlefield formation

Dueoksini is inside the junction niche, and the crown touches the ceiling pipe. The Wall-knockers stand along the wall from that junction toward the iron door. The brows of the line face the wall face that Dueoksini''s brow presses.

